   "replyText": "Nice to meet you, Sarah! I'm putting a little speaking-practice card on the screen next to me. It shows a simple way to introduce yourself: name, then one thing you like.\n\nSo you've said your name. Now try adding one thing you enjoy. What's something you like doing, Sarah?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "I live in a big house.",
   "startT": 24058,
   "endT": 25823,
   "audioSec": 1.77,
   "replyAudioLatencyMs": 2808,
   "replyTextEventLatencyMs": 2683,
   "heard": "I live in a big house.",
   "heardMessages": 1,
   "transcriptLatencyMs": 795,
   "queries": [
    {
     "status": 200,
     "firstContentMs": 1322,
     "totalMs": 2188,
     "chars": 229
    }
   ],
   "replyText": "That's a great sentence, Sarah — \"I live in a big house\" is clear and correct. The card on the screen has a small gap after the name. So try joining them: your name, then where you live. How would you say both together in one go?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "She has a red bag.",
   "startT": 43358,
   "endT": 45088,
   "audioSec": 1.73,
   "replyAudioLatencyMs": 3383,
   "replyTextEventLatencyMs": 3258,
   "heard": "She has a red bag.",
   "heardMessages": 1,
   "transcriptLatencyMs": 966,
   "queries": [
    {
     "status": 200,
     "firstContentMs": 1712,
     "totalMs": 2536,
     "chars": 211
    }
   ],
   "replyText": "Good sentence, Sarah — but let's keep practising you for now, not she. The card still shows your name gap. So start with \"My name is Sarah,\" then add \"and I live in a big house.\" Can you say both parts together?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "We play football on Friday.",
